# streamtop

HLS / DASH / IPTV diagnostics TUI.

## Architecture

- `ManifestPoller` ↔ UI via `tokio::sync::mpsc::unbounded_channel`
- UI must not block on network I/O; target ≥30 FPS render loop
- Show declared **video** FPS from HLS `FRAME-RATE` / DASH `@frameRate` in status + ABR ladder
- Fill missing res/FPS/codec from deep wire probe (`container_probe`); mark `[wire]`; log `[MISMATCH]` on conflict
- Segment panel shows DNS/TCP/TLS/TTFB (`network_trace`)
- HTTP / parse errors become events — never freeze the TUI
- English UI only

## HLS

- Cache ABR variants from master; highlight selected profile
- Direct media: "Single media stream (no master playlist)"
- Latency: PDT vs UTC, else `target_duration × 3`
- Ring buffers: last 60 latency / TTFB / bitrate samples

## Diagnostics

- RFC 8216 checks, origin stalling, CDN HIT/MISS, binary SCTE-35, ABR, SHI 0–100
- Virtual buffer, `--probe-headers`, LL-HLS PART/PRELOAD-HINT, A/V playlist drift
- `--compare URL1 URL2` split view; `--webhook` + `--alert-on` headless alerts

## UI

- Status: URL, LIVE/ESTIMATED, SHI, video FPS, latency, CDN, DVR, buffer
- Keys: `q` / `Esc` / `Ctrl+C`; `Space` → `diagnostics/<slug>_<timestamp>.json`; `r` reset; `c` curl; `?` help

## Safety

- Panic hook restores terminal
- Edition 2021 — `models`, `engine`, `ui`
